    ===================================================================================
    STATIC ASSETS - RESOLVED BY TASK 7.4 (deferrals 40 / 7.1-5 and 33 / 14.33)
    ===================================================================================
    Content\, Scripts\, Themes\DefaultClean\Content\, favicon.ico, ErrorPage.htm and
    FileNotFound.htm are STILL at their 3.90 locations, and that is now the decision rather
    than a deferral. In 3.90 System.Web's handler pipeline served them straight from the
    application root; ASP.NET Core's static-file middleware serves
    IWebHostEnvironment.WebRootFileProvider, i.e. wwwroot\ - which this application does not
    have, so nothing served at all after task 7.2.

    Task 7.4 chose the second of the two options the deferral offered: it repoints the
    PROVIDER instead of moving the files. Infrastructure\NopStaticFileProvider.cs is an
    allow-listed IFileProvider over the content root, installed onto
    IWebHostEnvironment.WebRootFileProvider by Infrastructure\NopStaticFilesExtensions.cs and
    registered from Program.cs as app.UseNopStaticFiles(). Relocation was rejected because
    three code paths require the files to remain physically under the content root:
    ThemeProvider enumerates MapPath("~/Themes/") for theme.config and keeps the resolved
    directory; CommonModelFactory PROBES MapPath("~/favicon.ico") before emitting a URL, so a
    relocated favicon would be served but never found; and PictureService WRITES generated
    thumbnails to MapPath("~/Content/Images/Thumbs"). Because the same provider instance is on
    WebRootFileProvider, IFileVersionProvider sees exactly the files that are served, which is
    what makes PageHeadBuilder's "?v=" cache busting fire - deferral 33 closed by the same
    line of code.

    App_Data\ (browscap.xml, GeoLite2-Country.mmdb, Install\*.sql,
    Localization\Installation\*.xml, Pdf\FreeSerif.ttf) is likewise read through
    CommonHelper.MapPath("~/App_Data/..."), which resolves against
    CommonHelper.BaseDirectory - set to the content root by
    builder.Environment.UseNopHostingEnvironment(builder.Configuration) at task 7.2
    (runtime deferral 5, mechanism supplied by task 6.5). It is deliberately OUTSIDE the
    static-file allow-list: System.Web blocked App_Data implicitly, ASP.NET Core does not, and
    App_Data\Settings.txt is the database connection string. What DID change at 7.4 is publish
    metadata - see the PUBLISH SHAPING block above, which is where the ~700 legacy <Content>
    entries are actually re-expressed (as `None Update` metadata rather than new items).

    CONFIG FILES. Web.Debug.config and Web.Release.config were DELETED by task 7.4 (unmodified
    XDT boilerplate; the Web SDK does not run XDT transforms). Web.config was reduced to the
    IIS/ANCM hosting shim, which is where the ImageResizer 'resizer' configSections
    declaration was removed per design section 7. Views\Web.config and
    Themes\DefaultClean\Views\Web.config are still on disk and remain TASK 7.5's to delete;
    7.4 only set CopyToPublishDirectory="Never" on them, because both declare a
    System.Web.WebPages.Razor <configSections> group that would cause an IIS 500.19 if
    published. Themes\DefaultClean\theme.config stays - ThemeProvider reads it, and IIS only
    parses files literally named web.config.
